{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9c92338431f97644511c3787d5462d54f6c00f51","text":"Withdrawn as unnecessary, and hugh owes nothing on it. I filed this proposal to give hugh's spoken UI instruction a ratifiable object for the implementing commit to rest on, having missed that one already exists: hugh ratified the web UI simplification design as the governing decision for the workroom UI at 25981e55, over proposal c26a7f57. That decision authorizes UI implementation on hugh's direction, and a concurrent planner lane is already using it as the basis for head 26e25bdf, so the pattern is settled.\n\nIt also covers this change on the merits rather than only by area. The ratified design says in terms: no count anywhere without being one click from exactly its rows. The \"N for you\" counter was exactly such a count -- one click took you to one row, not to the rows it counted -- so replacing it with the list is an instance of the adopted decision, not a new direction needing its own.\n\nThe implementing head now rests on 25981e55. The read-position design this proposal described is unchanged and will be carried in the artifact and put to a reviewer there, which is where it belongs; asking hugh to ratify a second UI decision would have added a board row for a question already answered."}